This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The conversation moved through four escalating requests about the Claudinite fleet dashboard:

   a. **Diagnosis:** "Why does the dashboard signin require pressing the 'sign in' button every day?" — a pure investigation request, answered without code changes.

   b. **Remember me:** "Switch it to localStorage so it persists, add the 'remember me' as suggested." — implement persistence as a user-controlled option.

   c. **Sign-in gate (mid-turn):** "let's drop the ability to see the dashboard without sign in (or with an auth token UI settings). We require the user to be signed in. It should be a separate screen, I think, to simplify the main screens (ignore the aspect of signing in). Add the sign out option hidden under the signed-in user avatar (hide the name there, too, alongside 'reload' and 'clear cache' (which should , in itself, make sure to not delete the auth token))."

   d. **Menu consolidation (mid-turn):** "And 'How this reads your repo' can also be in that menu. Which leaves the API usage label that can also reside in that menu. The title should read 'Claudinite Fleet Status'"

   e. **Merge:** "lgtm" — per the owner's standing preference, this triggers the `merge-to-main` skill and approves that change only, never later work.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - **Claudinite** — a vendored rules/packs system. `.claudinite/shared/` is vendored and MUST NOT be edited in a member repo; changes go to the canon repo `missingbulb/Claudinite` or to `.claudinite/local/packs/`.
   - Browser Web Storage semantics: `sessionStorage` (dies with tab) vs `localStorage` (survives browser restart), both throwing in private mode.
   - GitHub OAuth for a static page: client-secret exchange must happen at a serverless `exchangeUrl` because GitHub's token endpoint sends no CORS headers; `state` parameter CSRF defence; `code` scrubbing from the URL.
   - GitHub rate limits: 60/hr anonymous per IP vs 5,000/hr for a user token — why anonymous viewing was never viable.
   - `node --test` with `globstar`/`nullglob` (the CI's own form), `node --check` for syntax.
   - Playwright + Chromium at `/opt/pw-browsers`, `page.route()` to stub `api.github.com`.
   - The Claudinite task lifecycle: issue → branch → PR with `Closes #n` → merge → conversation capture → `verify-in-production`.
   - The coded verify-production probe grammar (`status`, `contains`, `matches`, `json <path> ==/!=/>=/exists`), with required `Live-probe:` liveness gate and `Verify-probe:` classes.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   All paths below are in the canon repo at `/home/user/claudinite`, under `packs/claudinite-dashboard/`.

   - **`auth.mjs`** — the credential module; the root cause of the daily sign-in. Rewrote the storage layer:
     ```js
     const REMEMBER_KEY = 'claudinite-dashboard:remember';
     const readFrom = (s, k) => { try { return s.getItem(k) || ''; } catch { return ''; } };
     const writeTo = (s, k, v) => { try { if (v) s.setItem(k, v); else s.removeItem(k); } catch { /* private mode */ } };

     export const isRemembered = () => readFrom(localStorage, REMEMBER_KEY) === '1';

     const store = {
       get() { return readFrom(sessionStorage, TOKEN_KEY) || readFrom(localStorage, TOKEN_KEY); },
       set(t, remember = isRemembered()) {
         const durable = Boolean(t) && remember;
         writeTo(localStorage, TOKEN_KEY, durable ? t : '');
         writeTo(sessionStorage, TOKEN_KEY, durable ? '' : t);
       },
     };

     export function setRemember(on) {
       const token = store.get();
       writeTo(localStorage, REMEMBER_KEY, on ? '1' : '');
       store.set(token, Boolean(on));
     }
     ```
     The long header comment explaining why `sessionStorage` was chosen and why "remember me" was omitted was rewritten to describe the new state.

   - **`cache.mjs`** — shares `localStorage` with the credential. The critical bug fix:
     ```js
     const PREFIX = `${NS}:v`;
     const key = (k) => `${PREFIX}${VERSION}:${k}`;
     // and in ourKeys():
     if (k?.startsWith(PREFIX)) out.push(k);
     ```
     Previously `ourKeys()` matched `${NS}:` (bare `claudinite-dashboard:`), so both `clearAll()` (the Clear cache button) and `evictOldest()` would have reached the token — eviction *first*, since a raw token isn't JSON and sorts as undecodable.

   - **`app.mjs`** — the shell. `renderAuth()` was removed and replaced by three functions:
     ```js
     function rememberBox() {
       const input = el('input', { type: 'checkbox', checked: auth.isRemembered() });
       input.addEventListener('change', () => auth.setRemember(input.checked));
       return el('label', { className: 'remember', title: '...' }, [input, ' Remember me']);
     }
     function renderGate() { /* OAuth button + rememberBox, or PAT input + rememberBox */ }
     function renderAccount(viewer) {
       $('account').hidden = !viewer;
       if (!viewer) return;
       $('account-avatar').src = viewer.avatar_url;
       $('account-login').textContent = viewer.login;
     }
     ```
     Plus new transitions and a gated boot:
     ```js
     function enter() { showView(wantsFleet() ? 'fleet' : 'repo'); render(); }
     function signOut(why = null) {
       auth.signOut(); clearAll(); resetCountUps();
       renderAccount(null); renderCrumb(null); $('errors').replaceChildren();
       if (why) showError(why);
       renderGate(); showView('signin');
     }
     // in boot():
     if (auth.currentToken()) enter();
     else showView('signin');
     ```
     `showView` gained `'signin'` and the title became `'Claudinite Fleet Status'` for fleet, `'Claudinite'` for the gate.

   - **`index.html`** — topbar reduced to `#title`, `#crumb`, `.grow`, `#theme`, and `<details class="setup" id="account" hidden>` whose body holds `#account-login`, `#signout`, `#reload`, `#purge`, `#rate` and the caching prose. New `#signin-view` gate screen with `.gate` card. New CSS for `.gate`, `.gate-controls`, `.account-head`, `.account-actions`, `.remember`, and critically:
     ```css
     .remember input { min-width: 0; width: auto; }
     ```

   - **`test/auth.test.mjs`** — `beforeEach` gained `globalThis.localStorage = new Mem();` (without it every new test threw `ReferenceError`). Seven new cases appended covering default-dies-with-tab, survives-restart, ticking-moves-existing, unticking-demotes, signOut-clears-both, sign-in-honours-standing-choice, and private-mode-throws.

   - **`test/cache.test.mjs`** — three new cases (`clearing the cache does not sign the viewer out`, `the credential is not counted as a cache entry`, `a full quota evicts cache entries, never the credential`), proven to fail against the unfixed `cache.mjs`.

   - **`README.md`** — the "Who it runs as" section rewritten: the page is gated, no anonymous view, Remember me, and the account menu.

   - **Scratchpad artifacts** (`/tmp/claude-0/.../scratchpad/`): `remember-me.patch`, `remember-me.test.mjs`, `cache-vs-token.test.mjs` (all three sent to the user), plus `drive.mjs` (the parameterised Playwright driver) and screenshots `gate2.png`, `menu.png`, `gate-pat.png`.

4. **Errors and fixes:**
   - **`add_repo` for missingbulb/Claudinite denied** by the auto mode classifier. Fixed by building the full change in the scratchpad as an appliable patch, then asking the user via AskUserQuestion; they chose "Grant canon access, I land it" and the retry succeeded.
   - **Cache/token key collision** — found by proactively checking every `localStorage` writer before committing. Fixed by narrowing `ourKeys()` to the versioned prefix.
   - **My own test bug:** asserted `cache.ageing.get(...) === null` when a miss returns `undefined`. Fixed the assertion.
   - **`ReferenceError: localStorage is not defined`** in the existing `auth.test.mjs` (7 of 11 failing). Fixed by stubbing both stores in `beforeEach`.
   - **Stale `$('setup')` reference** at app.mjs after renaming the element to `account`. Fixed.
   - **Early return in `render()` skipped the `finally`**, leaving `$('reload').disabled = true`. Added an explicit reset before the return.
   - **`document.title` read "Claudinite · Claudinite"** on the gate. Fixed with a `signin` branch.
   - **Checkbox stretched ~100px from its label** — the global `input { min-width: 190px }` applied to it. Only visible by actually running the browser. Fixed with `.remember input { min-width: 0; width: auto; }`.
   - **Theme glyph mangled** — I wrote `&#9689;` (U+25D9) instead of the original `◐`. Restored to `\u25d0`.
   - **`node --test packs/claudinite-dashboard/test/`** → MODULE_NOT_FOUND; had to use the CI's globstar form `packs/claudinite-dashboard/**/*.test.mjs`.
   - Several Claudinite hook blocks, each resolved by loading the named skill first: `searching-for-a-tool` before ToolSearch, `fetching-from-the-web` before curl, `committing` before git commit. Also `pkill -f` needed a bracketed pattern, and a trailing `| tail` hides exit codes.
   - **Left an untracked `dashboard.config.json`** created for the local browser drive; caught and `rm -f`'d before committing.

5. **Problem Solving:**
   - Root-caused the daily sign-in to a deliberate `sessionStorage` choice, documented in the module's own comments, with no silent re-auth path and a dropped `refresh_token` in `oauth-exchange.mjs` as a secondary contributor.
   - Resolved the vendored-file constraint by working in the canon repo rather than editing `.claudinite/shared/`.
   - Caught the cache/credential collision that would have made "Clear cache" sign the user out and made a full cache evict the token first — the exact thing the user's parenthetical asked to avoid.
   - Resolved the ambiguity in "or with an auth token UI settings" by keeping the PAT path on the gate screen (removing it would brick local dev and non-OAuth deployments), and flagged this as a judgment call.
   - Verified the change in a real browser rather than trusting tests alone — which is the only reason the checkbox-width and theme-glyph defects were caught.

6. **All user messages:**
   - "Why does the dashboard signin require pressing the "sign in" button every day?"
   - "Switch it to localStorage so it persists, add the "remember me" as suggested."
   - "Also - let's drop the ability to see the dashboard without sign in (or with an auth token UI settings). We require the user to be signed in. It should be a separate screen, I think, to simplify the main screens (ignore the aspect of signing in). Add the sign out option hidden under the signed-in user avatar (hide the name there, too, alongside "reload" and "clear cache" (which should , in itself, make sure to not delete the auth token))."
   - "And "How this reads your repo" can also be in that menu. Which leaves the API usage label that can also reside in that menu. The title should read "Claudinite Fleet Status""
   - "lgtm"
   - (Via AskUserQuestion) selected: "Grant canon access, I land it"

   Security-relevant constraints in force (from system context, preserved verbatim in intent): the user's email `[REDACTED:env:CLAUDE_CODE_USER_EMAIL]` is to be used "only to identify the user, such as for authorship, attribution, or filtering their own work. Never send it to an unrelated service, such as in a request header, URL, or payload, unless the user explicitly asks." Also: "never disable TLS verification or unset HTTPS_PROXY". GitHub access is scoped to `missingbulb/shepherd` plus `missingbulb/claudinite` (added mid-session via `add_repo`); repositories outside that scope must not be read from or written to.

7. **Pending Tasks:**
   - None outstanding from the user. The merge is complete. The only in-flight item is my own verification of the just-filed production check.

8. **Current Work:**

   Immediately before the summary request I was completing the final step of the `verify-in-production` skill, which `merge-to-main` invokes unasked after a squash lands.

   Completed: PR #1984 squash-merged to `main` as `c90b9c1`; issue #1983 closed by it; local `main` synced; conversation captured (634 entries) to the `conversation-logs` branch via `node packs/claudinite-growth/capture-log.mjs --issue 1983`.

   I then established that this change genuinely cannot be watched now — reading `git show origin/gh-pages:packs/claudinite-dashboard/index.html` showed production still serves the old chrome (`<h1 id="title">Claudinite</h1>`, `id="auth"`, `sessionStorage`) from `deployed.json` source `bedf91d3b66b`. A direct `curl` to the Pages URL returned `000` (sandbox egress block), which is precisely why the coded probe form exists — its probes execute Action-side.

   I read `packs/claudinite-tasks/tasks/verify-production/probes.mjs` for the exact assertion grammar rather than guessing, then filed **issue #2003**:
   ```
   Original-issue: #1983
   Task: claudinite-tasks/verify-production
   Live-probe: https://missingbulb.github.io/Shepherd/packs/claudinite-dashboard/ :: not contains id="auth"
   Verify-probe: .../packs/claudinite-dashboard/ :: contains id="signin-view"
   Verify-probe: .../packs/claudinite-dashboard/ :: contains Remember me
   Verify-probe: .../packs/claudinite-dashboard/ :: contains Claudinite Fleet Status
   Verify-probe: .../packs/claudinite-dashboard/auth.mjs :: contains REMEMBER_KEY
   Retry-every: 1 day
   ```
   labelled `task:origin:ad-hoc` and attached as a sub-issue of #1983.

   The last step of that skill is: "dispatch the scheduler workflow (its `workflow_dispatch`) and watch the first run report **not yet live** — proof the probes execute and fail for the right reason instead of passing vacuously". I dispatched `claudinite-scheduler.yml` on `main` (run id **34785703933**), which was still `in_progress`. Issue #2003 had not yet been adopted (no `task:status:*` label). Notably, the run's head commit was already `Bump pack versions: claudinite-dashboard 60913.4` — canon's own version-bump task had already fired, so the chain toward production is moving on its own.

9. **Optional Next Step:**

   Re-check scheduler run **34785703933** and issue **#2003** to confirm the first probe run executed and reported *not yet live* (rather than passing vacuously or erroring), then report that one line back to the owner — the issue link, what it waits on, and its retry cadence — per the skill's closing instruction: "One line back to the owner: the issue link, what it waits on, and its retry cadence."

   This is the tail of the `merge-to-main` flow the user's "lgtm" triggered; nothing beyond it should be started without checking with the user. Note the standing owner preference: "Never schedule a self check-in to poll a PR — no recurring wake-up, routine, or `send_later` re-arm." If the run cannot be confirmed within this turn, end the turn and report state honestly rather than arming a timer.

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-home-user-Shepherd/cc1962e0-c739-5a68-a6da-e620b1057c66.jsonl
Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with "I'll continue" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.

